TASK_DEADLINE lives in the core rather than in the Cloud Tasks queue because
both resume paths are bounded by it: Cloud Tasks enforces it as the dispatch
deadline, and the local timer uses the same value so a handler cannot be allowed
more time locally than in production.

update_time is timezone-aware UTC. A naive timestamp would compare wrongly
against a Spanner TIMESTAMP at the first daylight-saving boundary.
